From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] venus: no Metal export or import without the entry points

What: check vkGetMemoryMetalHandleEXT and
vkGetMemoryMetalHandlePropertiesEXT before calling them; without them the
export or import fails with a log line instead of calling NULL.
Why: they are looked up with vkGetDeviceProcAddr after device creation. A
driver built without VK_USE_PLATFORM_METAL_EXT (KosmicKrisp without Mesa's
macos platform) lists VK_EXT_external_memory_metal but returns NULL, and
the first blob a guest asked for crashed QEMU (SIGSEGV at 0 in
vkr_device_memory_export_blob): a guest-triggered host crash.
Upstream: upstreamable with the Venus-on-Metal patches (startergo's
homebrew-virglrenderer), not sent. Applies after
virgl-darwin-venus-heap-check.patch.
Test: KosmicKrisp built with -Dplatforms= (no macos) on the Mac mini:
vkmark in the guest fails with vk::Device::mapMemory ErrorMemoryMapFailed,
QEMU logs "metal export failed: the driver has no vkGetMemoryMetalHandleEXT"
and keeps running.

--- a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
@@ -510,6 +510,11 @@
          .pNext = NULL,
          .memoryTypeBits = 0,
       };
+      if (!vk->GetMemoryMetalHandlePropertiesEXT) {
+         vkr_log("metal import failed: the driver has no vkGetMemoryMetalHandlePropertiesEXT");
+         args->ret = VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
+         return;
+      }
       args->ret =
          vk->GetMemoryMetalHandlePropertiesEXT(args->device, handle_type, res->u.metal_heap, &mem_metal_props);
       if (args->ret != VK_SUCCESS)
@@ -657,6 +662,10 @@
          .memory = mem->base.handle.device_memory,
          .handleType = handle_type,
       };
+      if (!vk->GetMemoryMetalHandleEXT) {
+         vkr_log("metal export failed: the driver has no vkGetMemoryMetalHandleEXT");
+         return false;
+      }
       VkResult ret = vk->GetMemoryMetalHandleEXT(mem->device->base.handle.device, &metal_info, &metal_heap);
       if (ret != VK_SUCCESS || !metal_heap) {
          /* MoltenVK has a heap only with MVK_CONFIG_USE_MTLHEAP=1 */
